                        ],
                        "form": "underpointed"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "9aded4cd-8a31-4d85-a5e6-e4b753891512",
                        "entry_id": "45cc55b5-4ba6-3603-a60b-0cdb44572f76",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "underpointed"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "80ba73f4-a48e-3198-be61-168fcf0dbb4b",
                        "entry_id": "45cc55b5-4ba6-3603-a60b-0cdb44572f76",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To add a dot beneath a letter as a proofreading or diacritical mark."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b7ade9a3-df71-4941-8345-82d042608535",
                                "sense_id": "80ba73f4-a48e-3198-be61-168fcf0dbb4b",
                                "text": "Curiously, he does not underpoint letters to indicate deletion or insert letters above the line; he simply tries again."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "93ba9cb9-3109-44cf-99af-4ab5cab8d320",
                                "sense_id": "80ba73f4-a48e-3198-be61-168fcf0dbb4b",
                                "text": "One might disagree with the emendation, but that is beside the point: it would be inapposite to retain oftost and simply underpoint the first t, since the change presumably introduced by the scribe is not a mere alteration of form but a misapprehension, and this should be signalled by emendation and the use of italics."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c99b0353-bd1a-4cec-aa7d-347f5c01881a",
                                "sense_id": "80ba73f4-a48e-3198-be61-168fcf0dbb4b",
                                "text": "Klaeber's practice varies: he underpoints the inflectional vowel in bonan OngenÞēoẹs 1968ᵃ, but in oððe him OngenÞeowes 2475ᵃ he leaves off the macron and, evidently, assumes resolution."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "51744611-62ef-3ad2-9e3e-3efd14ae4de4",
                        "entry_id": "45cc55b5-4ba6-3603-a60b-0cdb44572f76",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To emphasize or call attention to a point within a discussion."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5105b92a-ff6b-45f8-a7fe-a7d0c00fbced",
                                "sense_id": "51744611-62ef-3ad2-9e3e-3efd14ae4de4",
                                "text": "I would like to underpoint that. Your statement is that your local in the heavy construction as contrasted to the other construction, is not on strike against anybody?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "848a9ff6-434d-4e76-89ed-e64bca036566",
                                "sense_id": "51744611-62ef-3ad2-9e3e-3efd14ae4de4",
                                "text": "I see a man who struggles for identity”: these lines underpoint the theme of this long poem which might be more effective without the “bondage of Rhyming”—to quote William Blake."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "19607ec3-740f-44ba-9160-6300b2698e32",
                                "sense_id": "51744611-62ef-3ad2-9e3e-3efd14ae4de4",
                                "text": "This again underpoints the vulnerability of climacteric women."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a2c93d99-657c-3a03-abc1-5d3a158b4826",
                        "entry_id": "45cc55b5-4ba6-3603-a60b-0cdb44572f76",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To point the underside."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "250f8341-bad8-47e8-80de-969f0f89e7ad",
                                "sense_id": "a2c93d99-657c-3a03-abc1-5d3a158b4826",
                                "text": "When the plates are firmly secured to the walls with the proper wall anchors all the interstices between the wedges should be underpointed with mortar."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a8445525-20bf-4521-b0da-b7e87eb04780",
                                "sense_id": "a2c93d99-657c-3a03-abc1-5d3a158b4826",
                                "text": "The most suitable material has proved to be the seconds or thirds types of Welsh slate laid on stout battens and well underpointed in haired mortar, gauged with cement."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "06a6e7c4-2615-4052-982c-f65b2ea6eaf9",
                                "sense_id": "a2c93d99-657c-3a03-abc1-5d3a158b4826",
                                "text": "Pantiles made from Bridgwater Clay must not be torched or underpointed, but the roof should be boarded and felted, battened and counterbattened."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "79f43624-e525-3188-87ed-b94013b791a1",
                        "entry_id": "45cc55b5-4ba6-3603-a60b-0cdb44572f76",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To include too few points."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8d23fb2e-0b05-473b-b216-56c15ab6c498",
                                "sense_id": "79f43624-e525-3188-87ed-b94013b791a1",
                                "text": "This gives us a good idea of how much water is down there and how many well-points we need to dewater the area,” Huber explains. “On our projects. we always try to overpoint rather than underpoint."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3aea60ec-e984-3a83-ae15-9148ee231386",
                        "entry_id": "45cc55b5-4ba6-3603-a60b-0cdb44572f76",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To indicate or focus on a position closer than the one that is intended."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c6707654-5955-4c43-be38-46cfa36a8575",
                                "sense_id": "3aea60ec-e984-3a83-ae15-9148ee231386",
                                "text": "If the patient then attempts to fix with the good eye, it will underpoint."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
